<<~ ahu slot=`#/floor-pinner-hand-back-the-vessel-pins-the-floor`>>

! Floor-Pinner hand-back: the vessel pins the floor

Branch `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--floor`, pushed. It merges the span head 594a22378 (the workbench lane).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/commits`>>

!! Commits
* `63bc695d9` lar:&#47;&#47;/vessel.pins.floor/accept-by-prior: the floor pin seam, both host bindings, the CLI, the announcement fold, wire-names, canon and the CHANGELOG.
* `600e0bcd2` lar:&#47;&#47;/span.meets.floor/merge-workbench: merges the span. It also fixes two test types and adds `workspace` to the `accepts` rows of `bag` and `wiki`. The CLI law accepts-track-the-handlers was already red on the span head. Only those two accepts rows changed, and no share verb was touched.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-shared-seam`>>

!! The shared seam (one implementation for both hosts)
`packages/lararium-mesh/src/floor-pin.ts`:
* ''Pin record.'' `{kind:"floor-pin", nexus, release, manifest}` at `<control>/floor-pin/<Nexus AID>` in the vessel's control home. It is keyed by Nexus only, so no face carries a pin.
* ''Genesis start.'' With no pin row, the pin is derived from `GENESIS_FLOOR_TIDDLER` (`release: null`). Nothing is written at boot, so a reboot writes nothing.
* ''Decision functions:''
** `floorStatusOf`: the pinned release, the newest head, whether it descends (fast-forward and its path), and any fork.
** `decideFloorAccept`: walks `prior` through the releases the board counts. It refuses with `floor-not-descendant` (rollback included), `floor-fork-unsettled` (names both heads), `floor-release-unknown` or `floor-no-release`. Accepting the release already pinned returns `moved:false` and writes nothing.
** `floorRemountDecision`: swaps live when the island offers it (`floorSwap` plus a swap port); otherwise it raises the reboot-pending alert and says why.
** `floorCidToMount` / `vesselFloorCid`: pick the floor a mount stands on (the vessel's only pin, or genesis).
* ''Composed doors.'' `readFloorStatus` and `acceptFloorRelease` run over ports named by capability: `home`, `rows`, `fetchCas`, `stage`, `mount`. Accept stages the manifest and snapshots into the CAS before it moves the pin. `raiseFloorAlert` places the reboot-pending `system-alert` into every live wiki.
* ''Supporting changes:''
** `foldFloorReleases` now also returns its `counted` set.
** `floorAnswerRows` is shared by `readFloorAnswer` and the browser.
** `IslandMsg_Manifest.floorCid` and `VesselIslandPoolCoreOptions.floorCid`: each activation reads the pin again.
** The tw5 kernel mounts `msg.floorCid` in place of the genesis witness. Plugin bytes are unchanged (sha256 of both plugin json files the same), so nothing goes into `genesis/unbaked.json`.
** `surface-recipe` takes a `floorCid` input.
* ''Announcement reader.'' `foldFloorAnnouncements` in `floor-announcement.ts` orders announcements by `prior`, starting from the line's opening or a held digest. Two heads read as `forked` with both named; recency never settles it. It sets aside `prior-unseen` and each read refusal.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/host-bindings`>>

!! Host bindings
* ''Node'' (`packages/lararium-node/src/commands/floor.ts`): binds the control home (`readControlHome`, which refuses on a locked vessel), the publication board replica, and the local CAS, with an optional `--porch` source for bytes.
** Store-door rows `floor-status` and `floor-accept` are rows of the place, not face rows. `floor-accept` needs a person's hand (`floor-needs-hand`).
** `floorAlert` is wired to `raiseFloorAlert(vmManager)`, and the pool's `floorCid` to `vesselFloorCid`.
* ''Browser'' (`packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-floor-pin.ts`): binds the control home the boot stood, the porch answer, and OPFS.
** The vessel result gains `floorStatus(baseUrl)` and `acceptFloor(baseUrl, release?)`, and the pool gets the same `vesselFloorCid`.
** When it cannot run a door it refuses by name: `floor-control-unread`, `floor-no-nexus`, `floor-no-genesis`, `floor-porch-silent`.
* ''CLI:'' `lares vessel floor status|accept [<release>] [--nexus] [--porch]` (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/floor.ts`, wired through `vessel.ts`).
* Neither host's island swaps its floor live today, so every accept raises the alert.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/wire-names`>>

!! Wire names (controller's parity row)
* <code>&#64;lararium/mesh/wire-names</code> is a new file with no imports and a package.json export. It holds GENESIS_SEED_FORMAT, ARRIVAL_FORMAT, FLOOR_MANIFEST_FORMAT, FLOOR_ANSWER_FORMAT, FLOOR_PIN_KIND and FLOOR_ANNOUNCEMENT_KIND.
* genesis-doc, floor-manifest, floor-answer, floor-pin, floor-announcement and node `pronaos-adapter` re-export from it, so each name has one owner.
* The web tests use the constants and parse the committed `genesis/seed.json` (vite `?raw`) through `readServedSeed`.
* ''Page paths touched (for the eyes-on walk):''
** `packages/lararium-web/src/genesis-anchor.ts`: imports the two constants; the hand-copied seed and arrival literals are gone.
** `packages/lararium-web/src/live-status.ts`: imports `ARRIVAL_FORMAT` in place of `"lar-arrival"`.
** `packages/lararium-web/tests/genesis-anchor.test.ts`, `packages/lararium-web/tests/arrival-relay.test.ts`.
** No page UI calls the floor doors yet.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/red-tests`>>

!! Red tests (each file run alone, `--maxWorkers=2`)
* ''mesh `tests/floor-pin.test.ts`'' (new). Covers: the pin starts at genesis and a status read writes nothing; accept fast-forwards over two releases and stages first; non-descendant refuses; a fork refuses naming both heads; a replay writes nothing; status reads the same after a reboot (automerge save, then load into a new Repo); a face switch moves no pin; remount swaps or alerts; the mount pick.
** Red proven against a mutated seam: 3 failures (non-descendant, fork, replay), then green once restored.
* ''mesh'' `floor-announcement` (4 fold tests), `wire-names` (new), plus floor-release, floor-answer and surface-mount.
* ''browser `tests/browser-floor-pin.test.ts`'' (new): the browser composition and a node-shaped binding give the same status, the same accept, and the same pin row byte for byte. Also covers stage plus alert, replay, fork, and the named refusals.
* ''node `tests/floor-door.test.ts`'' (new): both rows are place rows; accept is hand-only; the node binding calls the mesh decision and declares no live swap. Also ran swarm-verbs.
* ''web:'' genesis-anchor (adds the committed-seed test), arrival-relay.
* ''cli:'' laws, help-flags, vessel-surfaces, fresh-build-observe.
* Every touched test file passes again after the merge, and each typechecks under its package config.
* Red proof is weaker for some: the browser parity test, node floor-door, the announcement fold and wire-names went red only because their modules did not exist yet. I did not prove them against mutants.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gates`>>

!! Gates
* `pnpm -r build` and `tools/typecheck-witness.sh`: clean across all 11 projects, before and after the merge.
* Witnesses: bcc 807 ok; evergreen version 0/0 and narration 162/162 (three "slice 5" docblock notes trimmed); barrier, doctype and ahu-sections green.
* `browser-weld-witness`: C4.2 (reload) timed out 3 times in a row with the page edits in, then passed 3 times in a row (once traced, twice plain). A/B with the page edits reverted also passed. My read is a cold dev-server cache, not a defect, but the cause is unproven.
* `tree-clean-witness`: the run exited 1 and the tree stayed clean. I did not chase why.
* ahu-pair-parity needs the tree-sitter wasm build (not built here).
* No e2e and no full suites, by law.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/forks-i-decided`>>

!! Forks I decided (moʻolelo, each overrulable; also written in w26-floor-lane `#/the-vessel-pin`)
# The CLI is `lares vessel floor`, not top-level `lares floor`. The help's one-screen law (62 lines) is already full, the vessel door already says "never another top-level verb", and the pin belongs to the vessel.
# A genesis pin descends to every counted chain. The first release does not have to name the genesis manifest.
# A fork refuses even a named release that descends from the pin.
# A replay returns `moved:false` instead of refusing.
# Accept needs a person's hand (seat sessions refuse it), like a kahua lift.
# Mounts read the vessel's only pin. If two pins name different floors, the mount uses genesis and says so; it never chooses between Nexuses.
# Before writing the pin, accept fetches the floor whole and stages it in the vessel's own CAS, so the next boot never meets a missing floor.

<<~/ahu>>

